# Both spellings (annotated locals and direct call results) refuse `list * list` with SPY0222 (#1395).
Type 'list[int32]' does not support operator '*' with operand of type 'list[int32]'
# The regression symptom was the mis-type: `list * list` accepted as list[int], then SPY0220 assigning
# it to int. With the resolver agreeing with the fallback the operation is refused, so no SPY0220.
!SPY0220
